---
id: AP-007
type: rule
family: error-visibility
title: Console statement in production code
version: 1

severity: info
confidence: medium
spectrum_position: 2

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.ts, .tsx, .js, .jsx, .mjs, .cjs]
allowlist: ['**/*.test.ts', '**/*.spec.ts', '**/scripts/**', '**/cli/**', '**/explain/**']

detection:
  type: regex
  pattern: 'console\.(log|warn|info|debug)\s*\('

related: [AP-006]
enabled: true
opt_in: true
---

Replace this console statement with a structured logger that supports
log levels, context fields, and output routing.

Console output in production is the wrong observability channel — it
goes to stdout where nobody is watching, can leak sensitive data to
browser devtools, and can't be filtered, searched, or alerted on. If
this is intentional debugging, wrap it in a development-only check.
